les, each paired with an image of an analog clock. The left table lists classifications with confidence percentages: "analog clock" at 97.31%, "stopwatch" at 1.16%, "wall clock" at 0.88%, "barometer" at 0.60%, and "magnetic compass" a\t 0.03%. The right table shows "stopwatch" at 92.95%, "barometer" at 4.89%, "analog clock" at 1.07%, "wall clock" at 0.48%, and "magnetic compass" at 0.45%. A slider labeled "Epsilon: 2.16" is visible below the right table.␀)/K 44/P 10635 0 R/Pg 1597 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj10658 0 obj<</K 11271 0 R/P 10635 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj10659 0 obj<</K[29 11269 0 R 31]/P 10635 0 R/Pg 1597 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj10660 0 obj<</K[11263 0 R 11264 0 R]/P 10635 0 R/Pg 1597 0 R/S/L/Type/StructElem>>endobj10661 0 obj<</K[43<</MCID 4/Pg 1608 0 R/Type/MCR>>11261 0 R<</MCID 6/Pg 1608 0 R/Type/MCR>>]/P 10635 0 R/Pg 1597 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj10662 0 obj<</A 11260 0 R/Alt(Flow chart illustrating a process involving data and predictive modeling. It starts with "Training Data" leading to "Deep Learning Training," which then connects to "Predictive Model." The model outputs "Correct Labels." Separately, "Input Data" is affect\ed by "Noise," creating "Perturbed Data," which leads to "Evading" and results in "Falsified Labels." The "Evading" step also loops back to the "Predictive Model."␀)/K 2/P 10635 0 R/Pg 1608 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj10663 0 obj<</K 11259 0 R/P 10635 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj10664 0 obj<</K 8/P 10635 0 R/Pg 1608 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj10665 0 obj<</K 10/P 10635 0 R/Pg 1608 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj10666 0 obj<</K[11177 0 R 11178 0 R 11179 0 R 11180 0 R 11181 0 R 11182 0 R 11183 0 R 11184 0 R 11185 0 R 11186 0 R 11187 0 R 11188 0 R 11189 0 R 11190 0 R]/P 10635 0 R/Pg 1608 0 R/S/L/Type/StructElem>>endobj10667 0 obj<</K 65/P 10635 0 R/Pg 1612 0 R/S/H2/Type/StructElem>>endobj10668 0 obj<</K[67 11171 0 R 69 11172 0 R 71 11173 0 R