d representation. "Model Training" involves splitting the dataset, applying data augmentation, and optimizing the model. Finally, "Evaluation" calculates accuracy, precision, recall, and p-values with confiden\ce intervals.␀)/K 15/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1289 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj13825 0 obj<</K 14062 0 R/P 13801 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj13826 0 obj<</K 12/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1289 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj13827 0 obj<</K[14<</MCID 1/Pg 1293 0 R/Type/MCR>>]/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1289 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj13828 0 obj<</K 3/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1293 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj13829 0 obj<</K[5 14061 0 R 7]/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1293 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj13830 0 obj<</A 14060 0 R/Alt(Flow chart illustrating data processing steps for different modalities: text, audio, video, and interaction. - Text: Cleaning, Lemmatization, Tokenization \(BERT\), Padding, Truncation. - Audio: Spectrogram Conversion, MFCC/Chroma Features, Noise Reductio\n, Normalization. - Video: Frame Extraction, Cropping \(Dlib\), Resizing, Normalization. - Interaction: Feature Scaling, Temporal Feature Encoding, Behavioral Trend Extraction. Each modality follows a distinct path of processing steps.␀)/K 11/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1293 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj13831 0 obj<</K 14059 0 R/P 13801 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj13832 0 obj<</K 3/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj13833 0 obj<</K 5/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj13834 0 obj<</K 7/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj13835 0 obj<</K[14047 0 R 14048 0 R 14049 0 R 14050 0 R]/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/L/Type/StructElem>>endobj13836 0 obj<</K 25/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj13837 0 obj<</K 27/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj13838 0 obj<</A 11030 0 R/ActualText({\\text {Attention }}\\left \( {{\\text {Q}},{\\text {K}},{\\text {V}}} \\right \) \\, = {\\text { Sigmoid}}\\frac {{{\\text {QK}}^{T} }}{{\\sqrt {d_{k} } }}v)/Border[0 0 0]/K 29/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/Formula/Type/StructElem>>endobj13839 0 obj<</K[33 14046 0 R 35]/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj13840 0 obj<</A 14045 0 R/Alt(Flow chart illustrating a data processing pipeline. It begins with input sources: Twitter, Reddit, and DAIC-WOZ, providing text, image, and audio data. Text data undergoes text preprocessing, image data goes through image preprocessing, and audio data is \processed via audio preprocessing. User interaction data is also preprocessed. These processes lead to feature extraction, generating BERT embeddings, ResNet50 features, GRU features, and MLP features. Extracted features are then fused in the data fusion \stage, resulting in fused data. This data is used for final classification, producing a classification result, which is the output.␀)/K 2/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1302 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj13841 0 obj<</K 14044 0 R/P 13801 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj13842 0 obj<</K<</MCID 4/Pg 1302 0 R/Type/MCR>>/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj13843 0 obj<</K[14022 0 R 14023 0 R 14024 0 R]/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1302 0 R/S/L/Type/StructElem>>endobj13844 0 obj<</K 35/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1302 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj13845 0 obj<</K 37/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1302 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj13846 0 obj<</K 3/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1306 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj13847 0 obj<</K 5/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1306 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj13848 0 obj<</K 7/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1306 0 R/S/H2/Type/StructElem>>endobj13849 0 obj<</K 9/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1306 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj13850 0 obj<</K 11/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1306 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj13851 0 obj<</K[13 14020 0 R 15 14021 0 R 17]/P 13801 0 R/Pg 1306 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj13852 0 obj<</A 14019 0 R/Alt(Line chart titled "Loss Over Epochs" showing various loss metrics over 30 epochs. The y-axis represents loss values, ranging from 0 to 3,