ing vertical data flow. At the bottom is input block, from two path emerges: one path goes to two sequential Conv+ReLu layers, each layer having curved arrow indicating r\ecurrence. The second path is skip connection that bypasses the layers. Both path converge at addition node at top,which then goes to Output block.)/K 2/P 19948 0 R/Pg 661 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj19969 0 obj<</K 3/P 19948 0 R/Pg 661 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj19970 0 obj<</K 5/P 19948 0 R/Pg 661 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj19971 0 obj<</A 20103 0 R/Alt(A technical diagram of the UNet 3+ architecture illustrating deep supervision and full-scale skip connections. The model is structured in a U-shape with an encoder \(descending\) and a decoder \(ascending\).\n\n Encoder Path: Five circular nodes labeled X\Ee1 through XEe5 descend diagonally. Each node is associated with a filter count that doubles at each level: 64, 128, 256, 512, and 1024.\n\n Decoder Path: Four circular nodes labeled XDe4 through XDe1 ascend diagonally. Each decoder node maintains a cons\tant filter count of 320.\n\n Connectivity: Complex dashed lines represent 'Full-Scale Skip Connections.' Each decoder node \(XDe\) receives multiple inputs simultaneously from all higher-level encoder nodes \(via downsampling\), the same-level encoder no\de, and all lower-level decoder nodes \(via upsampling\).\n\n Deep Supervision: Each decoder node has a vertical block arrow labeled 'Sup' pointing to it, indicating where deep supervision can be applied during training.\n\n Flow: Data flows from encoder \to decoder shown by solid lines, the nodes in decoder also receive feature aggregation through skip connections shown by dashed lines.)/K 6/P 19948 0 R/Pg 661 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj19972 0 obj<</K[8 20097 0 R 10 20098 0 R 12 20099 0 R 14]/P 19948 0 R/Pg 661 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj19973 0 obj<</K 3/P 19948 0 R/Pg 664 0 R/S/H2/Type/StructElem>>endobj19974 0 obj<</K 4/P 1994