validation accuracy starts from 0.93 and ends at 0.95. The training accuracy in case of U2Net starts \from 0.87 and increase somewhat steadily to 0.98, while validation accuracy starts from 0.94 and ends at 0.95.\n\n The training dice in case of UNet3+ starts from 0.76 and increase somewhat steadily to 0.95, while validation dice starts from 0.63 and ends\ at 0.90. The training dice in case of Attention UNet starts from 0.72 and increase somewhat steadily to 0.98, while validation dice starts from 0.82 and ends at 0.91. The training dice in case of U2Net starts from 0.46 and increase somewhat steadily to 0\.95, while validation dice starts from 0.66 and ends at 0.91.)/K 2/P 19948 0 R/Pg 674 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj20009 0 obj<</K 3/P 19948 0 R/Pg 674 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj20010 0 obj<</A 20012 0 R/Alt(A grid of images showing skin lesions and their segmentation results. The first column displays original skin lesion photos. The second column shows the ground truth segmentation masks. The subsequent columns present segmentation results from different mo\dels: UNet3+, Attention-UNet, and U2Net. Each segmentation mask highlights the lesion area in white against a black background. The grid demonstrates the comparison of model performance in accurately identifying lesion boundaries.)/K 2/P 19948 0 R/Pg 677 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj20011 0 obj<</K 3/P 19948 0 R/Pg 677 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj20012 0 obj<</BBox[53.508 609.390998 386.404998 1108.253999]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj20013 0 obj<</BBox[219.955 223.686 757.955 516.780998]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj20014 0 obj<</ActualText(U^2)/K 60/P 20007 0 R/Pg 671 0 R/S/Span/Type/StructElem>>endobj20015 0 obj<</ActualText(U^2)/K 63/P 20007 0 R/Pg 671 0 R/S/Span/Type/StructElem>>endobj20016 0 obj<</K 19883 0 R/P 20005 0 R/S/Reference/Type/StructElem>>endobj20017 0 obj<</K 19884 0 R/P 20005 0 R/S/Reference/Type/StructElem>>endobj2001